WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:06.339
As one of the original Uncanny X-Men back
in 1963, Cyclops had a ton of potential.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:10.860
He's always been a key member of the mutant
squad, and his eyes can basically punch things,

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:14.249
so you'd think that would warrant a little
more respect around the Marvel Universe.

00:00:14.249 --> 00:00:18.270
But comic book writers have done a pretty
great job of making Scott Summers Marvel's

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:20.130
most hated hero.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:24.490
Let's take a look at the many ways this mutant
leader went from being kind of cool to kind

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:25.680
of a creep.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.600
A lousy lover

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.240
Cyclops has a pretty awful history when it
comes to how he treats women, whether it's

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:35.750
his girlfriend, cloned wife, or just some
random swamp floozy he's trying to move on

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:36.750
with.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:40.550
When he believes his longtime girlfriend,
Jean Grey, is dead from a volcanic explosion

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:44.460
in Uncanny X-Men #113, what does Scott do?

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:49.630
He gets over his grief pretty quick and starts
dating Marvel mainstay Colleen Wing.

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:54.041
Then, Cyclops straight-up dumps Wing once
he finds out that Jean is still alive, and

00:00:54.041 --> 00:01:00.630
proposes in Uncanny X-Men #136… but Jean
dies again as the Dark Phoenix an issue later.

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:06.149
By issue #144, he's back at it with some lady
in Florida named Lee Forrester.

00:01:06.149 --> 00:01:10.579
We'll chalk all that up to bad dating habits...but
it gets worse.

00:01:10.579 --> 00:01:15.429
Cyclops marries his dead fiancee's clone,
Madelyne Pryor, in Uncanny X-Men #175.

00:01:15.429 --> 00:01:19.310
And then he doesn't even treat his clone-wife
well.

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:23.549
It's eventually revealed that Pryor was a
tool in Mister Sinister's nefarious plans,

00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:27.780
but well before that revelation, Cyclops had
already started hanging out with Jean Grey,

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:32.310
back from the dead for the hundredth time
after hatching from a weird ocean cocoon,

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:37.650
leaving his wife at home with a young Cable
in some cyborg Huggies.

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:42.590
Madelyne does get her sort-of revenge, hooking
up with Cyclops' brothers, becoming the Goblin

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:44.509
Queen, and raising some hell.

00:01:44.509 --> 00:01:49.210
But when Madelyn dies later, Jean Grey actually
mourns harder than Scott does for his own

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:50.630
former wife and baby-mamma.

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:54.841
And we can't even get into which of these
Jean Greys were actually Jean Grey… and

00:01:54.841 --> 00:01:57.900
which were actually the Phoenix in Jean Grey
form.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.009
It gets complicated.

00:01:59.009 --> 00:02:03.520
Anyway, even after ditching his family for
a back-from-the-dead-for-real Jean Grey, he

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:06.389
decides his new relationship is getting a
little tired.

00:02:06.389 --> 00:02:09.829
Since, like, constant death and resurrection
isn't spicy enough.

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:14.720
Ever the loyal lover, Scott tries to liven
things up with some telepathic "therapy" from

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:17.590
Emma Frost... who's dressed up as Phoenix.

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:22.480
Since he's married to another immensely powerful
psychic, Jean quickly discovers his telepathic

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:23.480
tryst.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:24.720
So what does Cyclops do?

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:29.290
He tries to weasel his way out of it, claiming
their liaisons didn't count because they weren't

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:30.290
physical.

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:31.780
And did we mention this?

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:34.219
Somehow he also found time to hook up with
Storm.

00:02:34.219 --> 00:02:35.910
And who the heck is this?!

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:39.120
Maybe his eyes aren't the only part of his
body that he can't control.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:41.680
Maybe he should invest in some ruby quartz
underwear.

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:44.680
And that is why you fail as husband material,
Mr. Summers.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.519
Work over family

00:02:46.519 --> 00:02:50.980
Being the unpaid leader of Charles Xavier's
mutant squad is not an easy job, especially

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:53.459
when humans mostly just hate you constantly.

00:02:53.459 --> 00:02:58.410
Sometimes, an X-Man just wants to get married,
settle down, and spawn an omega-level mutant

00:02:58.410 --> 00:02:59.410
or two.

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:00.680
Not Scott Summers, though.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:05.350
Despite getting married to the aforementioned
Madelyne Pryor, Cyclops never left his super-villain

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:09.470
battling life behind, continually putting
the needs of the team before the needs of

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:10.680
his growing family.

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:15.760
If Cyclops was the sole mutant out there capable
of paying it forward, that'd be one thing.

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:20.239
But the X-Men and the Xavier Institute are
both overflowing with butt-kicking mutants.

00:03:20.239 --> 00:03:21.340
Like Dummy.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:22.340
And Beak.

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:23.340
And…

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:24.340
Glob Herman?

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:28.480
Anyway, even Storm confronted Scott at one
point over his dereliction of family duties.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:29.480
His response?

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:34.140
Well, he challenged her to a duel, of course…
and he lost, even though Storm didn't use

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:35.180
her powers.

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:36.670
He built a murder squad

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:41.180
The mutant team known as X-Force was always
a bit rough around the edges, and often found

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:45.489
themselves at odds with both the X-Men and
the government, as well as the anti-mutant

00:03:45.489 --> 00:03:46.650
groups they battled.

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:50.689
None of these problems were helped by Cyclops
being an extremely divisive leader.

00:03:50.689 --> 00:03:56.579
In Uncanny X-Men #493, Scott Summers shows
some early signs of being a total fascist

00:03:56.579 --> 00:03:59.849
by reorganizing the team to kill his own son,
Cable.

00:03:59.849 --> 00:04:03.760
As if tracking and murdering your own kid
wasn't bad enough, he took the traumatized

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:06.439
teenage killing machine, X-23, on board.

00:04:06.439 --> 00:04:10.900
He encouraged her murdery tendencies rather
than helping her reform, which went against

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:12.269
Wolverine's wishes.

00:04:12.269 --> 00:04:15.599
And that, of course, earned him a good ol'
Logan punch to the face.

00:04:15.599 --> 00:04:16.980
"Prove it."

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:19.050
"You're a d---."

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:23.860
And naturally, Cyclops disavows any knowledge
of X-Force's actions — until he's caught

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:25.790
red-handed by the rest of the X-Men.

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:29.930
And it's far from the last time Cyclops would
be a dangerous extremist.

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:31.850
He brought Phoenix back

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:35.220
Over the years, the X-Men have dealt with
more than their fair share of ridiculously

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:36.500
powerful beings.

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:39.980
But few of their foes matched the devastating
Phoenix Force.

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:44.000
Cyclops didn't just deal with this cosmic
firestorm on numerous occasions…he basically

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:46.310
married the woman who was possessed by it.

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:50.510
But despite enjoying far too much face time
with a creature that once destroyed an entire

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:55.220
populated world out of spite, Scott Summers
decided to welcome it back to Earth during

00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:57.020
the Avengers vs. X-Men event.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:05:01.910
The Phoenix Force breaks apart and chooses
to join with him and four fellow mutants.

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:06.480
But it turns out that just one part of the
Phoenix Force isn't enough, so he steals some

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:11.640
from his on-again, off-again girlfriend Emma
Frost, making himself nearly omnipotent.

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:16.630
Insane with power, Cyclops goes full-Dark
Phoenix and tries to kill pretty much everyone.

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:21.720
In the penultimate issue, the altruistic Professor
X tried to help Cyclops escape his cosmic

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:22.730
power trip.

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:27.100
But Scott declined, forcing Xavier to lay
the psychic smack-down on him.

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:32.120
Unfortunately, even an omega-level mutant
like Professor X is no match for the intergalactic

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:36.550
might of the Phoenix, and he's absolutely,
totally murdered by Cyclops.

00:05:36.550 --> 00:05:40.960
All of this even before he's taken over by
the Phoenix Force, so he can't even really

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:43.690
blame the alien entity for being a jerkbag.

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:48.370
In the end, he's stripped of his powers, and
Scott winds up in prison, moaning about his

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:49.580
public image.

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:52.000
Because it's all about him, right?

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:53.400
From hero to radical

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:57.650
Merging himself with the corrupting Phoenix
Force, and having it literally punched out

00:05:57.650 --> 00:06:02.210
of him, would probably be enough to make most
superheroes go cold turkey for a while.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:04.580
But Cyclops never seems to learn his lesson.

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:10.300
Many readers agree that the downward spiral
began with 2000's X-Men #97, when he merged

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:14.180
with Apocalypse, but things only got worse
after the Phoenix thing.

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:19.840
In Avengers vs. X-Men: Consequences, Magneto
and his crew bust Cyclops out of super jail.

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:24.500
The X-Man then goes on to declare a mutant
revolution, threatening anyone and everyone

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:26.490
with the wrong end of an optic blast.

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:30.930
In the months following his "death" in Death
of X, Summers even inspires a crew of brutal

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:36.110
mutant thugs to carry on his genocidal uprising,
a not-so-merry band that calls themselves

00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:37.570
"The Ghosts of Cyclops."

00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:39.810
You guys, Cyclops isn't just a jerk.

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:41.700
He's kind of a full-fledged war criminal.

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:46.460
And that includes an earlier incident from
Secret Invasion, where he intentionally infects

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:51.610
an invading force of Skrulls with the Legacy
virus, which is incredibly bad news, and had

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:54.900
the potential to spread just about everywhere,
very quickly.

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:57.740
Aren't there, like, laws about this kind of
thing?

00:06:57.740 --> 00:06:59.960
He incited war from beyond the grave

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:04.370
When Cyclops discovers that a weird fog has
killed the mutants on Muir island during the

00:07:04.370 --> 00:07:09.580
Death of X storyline, including Multiple Man
Jamie Madrox, fingers are immediately pointed

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:12.780
at The Inhumans, and their transformative
"Terrigen mists."

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:18.390
In an effort to destroy the mutant-blighting
mists, Cyclops recruits a small army, including

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:23.440
a chemical whiz kid named Alchemy who pretty
much wants nothing to do with a mutant war,

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:28.040
and ends up getting killed while neutralizing
just one of a few of the toxic fart clouds.

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:32.780
At the end of the battle, Cyclops is killed
by Black Bolt's ridiculous singing voice,

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:36.420
becoming a martyr for everything wrong with
the pro-mutant cause.

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:39.000
Except Cyclops wasn't even alive at the time.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:43.470
He was killed by the mutant plague before
the first issue even ended, and from then

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:47.610
on, he was only a deranged psychic projection
created by Emma Frost.

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:52.240
Sadly, dead men have no PR departments, so
it's easy to understand why so many people

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:54.000
ended up hating Cyclops.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:55.800
But his worst crime of all?

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:57.430
He's named Cyclops….

00:07:57.430 --> 00:07:58.430
And he has two eyes.

00:07:58.430 --> 00:07:59.930
What a freakin' liar.

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:01.440
Thanks for watching!

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:04.470
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:06.770
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

